{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/351126-15-years-of-reckoning","id":351126,"title":"15 Years of Reckoning","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-26T18:15:53-08:00","id":351126,"title":"15 Years of Reckoning","content":"I know i know..i know theres a lot of hate against Hunter the Reckoning, but to be honest..its my favorite game on the World of Darkness, its always been. its the little cry of Hope in the middle of the darkness..and yes, theres some flaws and some things that in retrospective are very &quot;Why?&quot; (like how each game has at least one 'Hunters' group or faction) but the imbued where the will of God (?) and a force to Reckon when the Final Days came..Thats why, i would like to help backing this proyect, even if its a fan proyect..but i really wish we could pull something up.<br /> What would you change? what would you add?<br /> <br /> personally, i think it woudl be interesting for a book to have both Hunters (all the creeds, infernals, missing creeds and such) and as well a quick description on how to play Twilight Project, Leopold and other types of Hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T20:24:34-08:00","id":351236,"title":"","content":"Yes! Hunter the Reckoning is, and always will be my favorite WoD game. There are a few things that I would change(and the changes would be easy), but overall the game is fantastic. To this day, I STILL play the game with a few friends. I'm anxiously awaiting Hunter 20th. I know it's coming. Eventually. I know it's not currently planned, since 2019 is still a ways away. But I also know it will be amazing.<br /> <br /> I would keep Project Twilight, SoL, Arcanum, etc. out of Reckoning. To me, they just don't belong there. There could be a chapter about how they work together, which was already done in the book First Contact.<br /> <br /> I think someone on here had an idea about doing something about their power levels, and maybe dropping a tad bit of the Christian mythology surrounding it(not dropping it entirely).<br /> <br /> Also, something would have to be changed about Hunter Net, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 12-26-2014, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T20:40:00-08:00","id":351250,"title":"","content":"Didn't the game come out and name the Scarlet Queen and Ebon Dragon as the forces behind the Imbued? That's a bit far from Christian tradition, even if there were some peripheral (and very contradictory and confusing) ties to Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T20:45:49-08:00","id":351258,"title":"","content":"A lot of hate against HtR? Personally I've encountered very little hatred towards HtR. In my experience KotE, DtF and CtD get the lion's share of hatred among OWoD lines. In fact I haven't encountered anyone that's hated HtR. The most I've met are people who don't care about HtR. They don't hate it but it doesn't appeal to them either.<br /> <br /> As for changes to HtR I have only one, artwork that is actually consistent with the material.<br /> <br /> And for non-Imbued hunters, there actually is a book for playing them. It's called Hunters Hunted II. HtR is not HtV. It's about the Imbued, those men and women that have been chosen and blessed, or perhaps cursed, with the knowledge of the monsters of the world and the power and will to do something about them. The non-Imbued hunters are their own thing, having existed long before HtR came out and generally have about as much to do with them as a member of the Society of Leopold does with an agent of Project Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T20:53:50-08:00","id":351284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/351126-15-years-of-reckoning?p=351250#post351250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't the game come out and name the Scarlet Queen and Ebon Dragon as the forces behind the Imbued? That's a bit far from Christian tradition, even if there were some peripheral (and very contradictory and confusing) ties to Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember correctly they are the last two angels on Earth which also adds to the links with the Kuei-Jin, implying that the Wan Xian, the Ten Thousand Immortals that once protected the Middle Kingdom only to become corrupted by their power and cursed into the Kuei-Jin, were the first Imbued.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T23:40:13-08:00","id":351390,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'd like to Hunter removed from the End Times baggage, I mean even Werewolf is pulling back on that with the prophecy of the Phoenix Make them something that has always happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T04:19:24-08:00","id":351499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/351126-15-years-of-reckoning?p=351250#post351250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't the game come out and name the Scarlet Queen and Ebon Dragon as the forces behind the Imbued? <b>That's a bit far from Christian tradition</b>, even if there were some peripheral (and very contradictory and confusing) ties to Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't directly talking about that. More of what was actually contained in the 24+ books contained in the Hunter the Reckoning line. The references and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T05:20:36-08:00","id":351540,"title":"","content":"That was actually one of the things I loved about the game, and also that it added to the mystery of the Imbuing and built into the idea of the End. It gave the setting character, but wasn't so stifling that it required, or rather restricted player choice.<br /> <br /> So, I'd say keep it, but not actually answer the question at the end, which is very likely what would happen in a H20 book, as they tend to remove the Time of Judgment aspects. However, there is also a very strong suggestion that Hunters are being Imbued as a direct reaction to The End, so I'm not sure I'd actually want that removed.<br /> <br /> Also, something that needs pointed out, Hunter's didn't just show up in 1999ish out of nowhere. They have actually been present before (in Dark Ages Inquisitor), and in small numbers pop up throughout history.<br /> <br /> I'd actually love a book that basically focused on the Year of the Hunter, combining Hunter's Hunted Project Twilight, the Arcanum, and some HtR. To me, this seems like a very dang solid way to continue the 20th Anniversary line, but kind of doing what the main books have done and combining a lot of the material into one book and then updating them to the modern world.<br /> <br /> I' pretty sure that HtR outsold both Wraith and Changling, so I'm confident that when the time comes, we will see a H20, and from there, I think it will really be about how people back it. Being that Hunter is sort of the opposite of both CtD and WtO in that they got 1st Ed and 2nd Ed, but no Revised, HtR only got a Revised edition, ad so not sure just how much it would need to change/update. As far as technology goes, it's still pretty up to date with a few obvious tweeks. If I recall, it already talks about the risks of cell phone videos, and the assumption is that monsters just will not let these things be taken seriously on the internet. It already contains Text Messages, easy internet access, and &lt;YouTube&gt;. In the states, I'd think one of the few real changes might be things like the Patriot Act?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1